    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through the exchange around Not My Pâté line by line and unpack how the Russian works.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Неплохо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Not bad.' Chef Barinov delivers a punchy one-word reaction built around the Russian word meaning 'not bad'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Да?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Huh?' Max asks this with a single word meaning 'yes', using rising intonation to turn it into a quick question.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Только это не мой паштет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Only this isn't my pâté.' Russian omits the present-tense verb 'to be' here, linking 'only' directly with 'pâté', combining 'only' with 'pâté'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Как?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What?' Max asks this with a single word meaning 'how', using rising intonation to turn it into a quick question.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Та же консистенция.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Same texture.' Russian omits the present-tense verb 'to be', connecting 'that' directly with 'consistency'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "И состав я подобрал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And I got the ingredients right.' Here Max anchors the line on the word meaning 'roster' and builds the thought around 'to pick up'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Подождите.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Wait.' Max replies with a single verb form meaning 'wait' — in Russian, the verb ending alone carries the subject and tense.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Что входит в ваш паштет?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What goes into your pâté?' The question word for 'what' comes right at the start, followed directly by 'pâté'.",
