    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Пойдём.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Let's go.' Chef Barinov delivers a punchy one-word reaction built around the Russian word meaning 'let's go'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Посмотрим.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Take a look.' Chef Viktor replies with a single verb form meaning 'have a look' — in Russian, the verb ending alone carries the subject and tense.",
